`parse_sidecar(path)` (128-248) reads TOML via `tomllib`, branches on top-level table (`experiment`/`benchmark`/`validation`/`debug`), builds the `Sidecar`. Optional blocks are parsed conditionally: `[reproduction]` at 173-186, `[controls]` at 188-198 — each guarded by `if <block> in data`/truthy check, populates the dataclass, and logs `logger.warning` for unknown keys (no hard failure). `_str_list()` (113-125) coerces list-or-string TOML fields (used for `claim_discriminates`/`claim_isolates` — an extension pattern to reuse).

`parse_sidecar(path)` (128-248) reads TOML via `tomllib`, branches on top-level table (`experiment`/`benchmark`/`validation`/`debug`), builds the `Sidecar`. Optional blocks are parsed conditionally: `[reproduction]` at 173-186, `[controls]` at 188-198 — each guarded by `if <block> in data`/truthy check, populates the dataclass, and logs `logger.warning` for unknown keys (no hard failure). `_str_list()` (113-125) coerces list-or-string TOML fields (used for `claim_discriminates`/`claim_isolates` — an extension pattern to reuse).

`evaluate_outcome(sidecar, result)` (321-354): builds a synthetic DuckDB `SELECT <cols> FROM (SELECT ...)` from the result dict (each value SQL-literal-encoded via `_sql_literal`, 329-344), then for each `outcomes.*` entry runs `SELECT (condition) FROM (...)` and returns the first label whose condition evaluates truthy; `"unknown"` if none match; raises `SidecarError` on malformed SQL.

