## 2. `src/bathos/runner.py` — `bth run` execution model

`run_script()` (188-575) flow: resolve campaign → find script path → compute `script_sha256` → `resolve_sidecar`/`parse_sidecar` (254-266) → resolve agent mode → capture git state → **pre-flight gate** at line 299-311: `gate_check()` (imported from `prereg.py`) is called only `if is_in_enforced_dir(script_path) and not no_sidecar`; on `not gate_result.ok` it prints the JSON error payload and **returns exit code 1 without ever spawning the subprocess** — this is the "refuse to proceed" mechanism. `gate_check` (in `prereg.py` 392-476) checks, in order: sidecar missing → sidecar invalid (via `validate_sidecar`) → sidecar-hash drift (deny in autonomous, warn in collaborative) → `check_first_of_kind` (autonomous only) → `adversarial_check` presence (autonomous only). Each failure returns a `GateResult(ok=False, error_payload=GateErrorPayload(error_code: GateErrorCode, phase, taxonomy_label, errors, agent_mode, resolution_hint, gate_schema_version=2))`. `GateErrorCode` enum (22-34) is the taxonomy to extend for a new differential-related pre-flight code (e.g. reserved slots exist: `RESULT_SCHEMA_MISMATCH`, `OUTCOME_AMBIGUOUS`).

`run_script()` (188-575) flow: resolve campaign → find script path → compute `script_sha256` → `resolve_sidecar`/`parse_sidecar` (254-266) → resolve agent mode → capture git state → **pre-flight gate** at line 299-311: `gate_check()` (imported from `prereg.py`) is called only `if is_in_enforced_dir(script_path) and not no_sidecar`; on `not gate_result.ok` it prints the JSON error payload and **returns exit code 1 without ever spawning the subprocess** — this is the "refuse to proceed" mechanism. `gate_check` (in `prereg.py` 392-476) checks, in order: sidecar missing → sidecar invalid (via `validate_sidecar`) → sidecar-hash drift (deny in autonomous, warn in collaborative) → `check_first_of_kind` (autonomous only) → `adversarial_check` presence (autonomous only). Each failure returns a `GateResult(ok=False, error_payload=GateErrorPayload(error_code: GateErrorCode, phase, taxonomy_label, errors, agent_mode, resolution_hint, gate_schema_version=2))`. `GateErrorCode` enum (22-34) is the taxonomy to extend for a new differential-related pre-flight code (e.g. reserved slots exist: `RESULT_SCHEMA_MISMATCH`, `OUTCOME_AMBIGUOUS`).

`check_reproduction_prerequisite(requires_pass_stem, catalog_dir)` (prereg.py 296-353) is the closest "F3-style prerequisite" precedent — warm-then-cool-tier lookup for `outcome='pass'` on a stem; not currently wired into `gate_check` itself (called from elsewhere, presumably `campaigns.py`/CLI).

