## 5. Existing positive-control / differential / sanity concepts

## 5. Existing positive-control / differential / sanity concepts

`grep` across `src/bathos/*.py` for `positive_control`, `differential`, `sanity`, `invalid_measurement`, `min_effect` returned **no matches** — none of these concepts exist yet anywhere in the codebase. The closest existing analog is `ControlsBlock` (`sidecar.py` 50-54, `[controls]` block: `positive_outcome`/`negative_outcome` — lists of outcome *labels*, not a re-execution gate) and `[reproduction].requires_pass_stem`/`requires_parity_stem` (prerequisite-run gating by stem). Validation for both lives in `src/bathos/validate.py`: `validate_reproduction_block()` (113-149) and `validate_controls_block()` (151-176+), both invoked from the main `validate_sidecar()` at lines 343-349, and both follow the "return `[]` if block absent, else check each field" pattern — the template to follow for a new `validate_differential_block()`.
